 and preferably derive call partitioning from fuzz input to cover its stateful incremental-update protocol. None of these actions was needed in S0.","evidence":["The source file is entirely new and S0 has no matching declaration.","S1's update_u32! accepts a caller-supplied roslice base.u8 and mutates persistent hasher state.","H0's compile-time module selection and GIF-only call path cannot reach the new entry point."]},"explicit_failure":false,"delta_attribution":"NEW","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":99,"reason":"Within the stable scope of the newly added xxHash32 public hashing capability, S0 had no API to expose, while S1 adds a caller-driven, stateful entry that unchanged H0 cannot compile or invoke. This changes the same-scope gap from absent to present and creates concrete compile-enablement, construction, buffer-supply, and call-sequencing obligations; therefore the delta is NEW."}
